diff --git a/NOTES.md b/NOTES.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7c43d5b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Credit control – implementation notes
+
+Nothing was run: there is no shell or database here, so none of this was executed or tested. Review and test it before shipping (see "Not done / to verify").
+
+## What webERP already had, and what I built on
+
+webERP already models a credit status: `debtorsmaster.holdreason` → `holdreasons.dissallowinvoices` (1 = no invoicing, 2 = "watch"). Order entry and counter sales read it, but:
+
+- `CreditStatus.php` could only create 0/1, so **watch could not be defined**. It now has a 3-way select (OK / watch / stop).
+- Stop was enforced only at customer selection in `SelectOrderItems.php`, in `CounterSales.php` and in `SpecialOrder.php`. It was **not** checked when an order was saved, at dispatch and invoicing, in recurring orders, EDI or the API.
+- In `SelectOrderItems.php` a customer on watch was refused on the second request (`dissallowinvoices == 0` test). Fixed.
+- `CustomerInquiry.php` showed "ACCOUNT ON HOLD" for watch (`!= 0`), and `-1` (the column default) also counted as "on hold". Fixed. Update 44 turns existing `-1` into `0`, and the demo hold reasons now carry explicit values.
+
+So stop/watch = the existing holdreason, not a second flag. No parallel status exists to drift.
+
+## What was built
+
+**Schema** (update `sql/updates/44.php`, `install/sql/tables/*`, `install/sql/data/*`, `install/sql/demo.sql` — all four places the project keeps schema/seed)
+- `debtorsmaster.nextreviewdate, nointerest, nofees`; `debtortrans.disputed`; `salesorders.creditheld, creditreleased`.
+- New tables: `creditlog` (append-only history of every credit action), `creditreviews`, `dunningstages`, `dunningletters`, `creditcharges` (unique per customer/month/kind), `writeoffs`.
+- Transaction types 45 (interest and late fee), 46 (waiver), 47 (write-off). Security tokens 21 (credit control) and 22 (approval of large write-offs), granted to roles 8 and 6 (21 only) — adjust in User Roles. Scripts, menu items (AR module), config values, default three reminder stages, stop/watch/normal hold reasons.
+- Existing customers get next review = today + 12 months at upgrade. Credit control then puts the spreadsheet stop list on stop in Customer Credit (or via `Z_ImportDebtors.php` with a hold reason).
+
+**Shared code** `includes/CreditControlFunctions.php`: status lookup, history log, held-order check, overdue invoices, and the posting of charges/waivers/write-offs (debtortrans + gltrans + custallocns, same allocation and exchange-difference rules as `CustomerAllocations.php`).
+
+**Pages**
+- `CustomerCredit.php` – per customer: record a review (limit changes in the same transaction), change status with a reason, exemptions, disputed invoices, notes (collection agency etc.), full history. Reps see their own customers read-only; a customer login sees only its own balance, reminders and charges (no status, limit or internal history).
+- `CreditControlReport.php` – review due, over limit (and by how much), watch/stop; filter by rep and currency; home-currency totals; reps restricted to their own.
+- `CreditHeldOrders.php` – held over-limit orders, open orders of customers on stop (release with a reason), open orders on watch.
+- `DunningRun.php` / `DunningStages.php` – preview, untick to exclude, send; stages/days/wording configurable.
+- `CreditCharges.php` – month-end preview, confirm, post; waiver with reason.
+- `BadDebtWriteOff.php`, `CreditWriteOffReport.php` – write-off, approval above a limit, report.
+- `CreditReconciliation.php` – customer balances vs debtors control account, with lists explaining a difference.
+- `CreditControlSettings.php` – review months, hold-over-limit, reminder spacing, rate, fee, min days, GL accounts, approval limit.
+
+**Enforcement of stop / hold** (every route that creates or invoices an order)
+- `DeliveryDetails.php` (new and changed orders, checked again at save), `ConfirmDispatch_Invoice.php` (no dispatch/invoice of an order on stop or held, unless released), `RecurringSalesOrdersProcess.php` (skips; template left to catch up), `EDIProcessOrders.php` (not created, reported in the advice email), `api_salesorders.php` (header refused, lines hold the order, invoicing refused; new error codes 1174/1175), `SelectOrderItems.php` (customer is cleared on stop; the web shop customer sees only "account on hold").
+- Over-limit orders are accepted but held (`creditheld`) from the screen, API, EDI and recurring paths; a recurring auto-invoice is not run for a held order.
+
+**Other existing pages changed**: `Customers.php` (limit and status read-only and ignored on save for anyone without token 21, change logged, new customers get a review date and an audit row), `api_customers.php` and `Z_ImportDebtors.php` (review date on insert), `Z_ChangeCustomerCode.php` (new columns and the new tables follow the new code), `AgedDebtors.php` (limit, status, last reminder stage), `CustomerInquiry.php`, `SelectCustomer.php` (status banner, link), `CreditStatus.php`.
+
+**Staff guide** `doc/Manual/ManualAccountsReceivable.html`: new Credit Control section (all items in BRD 4.1, plus the short note for sales staff) and corrected the old "limit is memorandum only" text.
+
+## Decisions on the open questions
+
+1. **Interest**: simple annual rate, set once in the home setting (not per currency/country). Applied per month to undisputed invoices overdue ≥ N days at month end, for the days of the month overdue.
+2. **Late fee**: one flat fee per customer per month, defined in home currency and converted to the customer currency at the current rate.
+3. **No interest on interest/fees**: only invoices (type 10) bear interest.
+4. **After the final letter**: flag only (the run page marks the final stage); an optional setting puts the customer on stop automatically. Default off.
+5. **Over-limit orders from any route**: held for approval, not rejected (matches BR-10). The existing `CheckCreditLimits = 2` "prohibit" still rejects at entry if an installation uses it.
+6. **Write-off threshold** 1,000 in home currency by default, Finance Director (token 22) approves above it. No Financial Accountant sign-off built in; give the accountant token 22 if wanted. A FD raising a write-off posts it directly.
+7. **Written-off debt later paid**: not automated. The manual says to take it as an unallocated receipt; recoveries accounting needs a decision by Finance.
+8. **Reps are told the stop/watch reason** (they asked for it in the user stories); customers are told only "on hold".
+9. **Letter languages**: English only; the wording is editable per stage.
+10. **Watch not shown to customers.**
+11. **Both credit controllers away**: anyone Finance gives token 21 can act; nothing special is built.
+12. **Branch groups**: the limit is per customer (debtor); branches share it.
+
+## Other judgement calls
+
+- Reminder "episode": letters sent since the oldest currently overdue invoice fell due count as the current sequence; a customer climbs one stage per run and nothing is sent twice within `DunningMinDaysBetween` days. Eligibility is recomputed at send.
+- Posted charges use new transaction types so they print as separate, named items on statements and in the portal and cannot be confused with invoices. Waivers/write-offs allocate to the items they clear.
+- Interest uses today's balances with days overdue measured at month end, so run it right after month end.
+- Customers can't be sent a letter if their email send fails; it is then not recorded.
+
+## Not done / to verify
+
+- **Untested** – syntax, SQL and the update script have not been run. Check `44.php` on an upgrade and a fresh install (with and without demo data).
+- The legacy `sql/demo.sql` and `sql/mysql/*` upgrade files were not touched (legacy upgrade path).
+- `Z_ChangeGLAccountCode.php` does not rename the three new config values holding GL account codes (`InterestIncomeAct`, `LateFeeIncomeAct`, `BadDebtAct`).
+- `EDIProcessOrders.php` already has `if ($CreateOrder = true)` (assignment); I left it and added the stop check next to it.
+- Picking-list printing is not blocked for customers on stop; invoicing is.
+- Credit-limit changes made directly by `Z_ImportDebtors.php` (admin utility) are not logged.
+- Existing pre-update sessions keep running new code against the old schema until users log in again (project-wide upgrade behaviour).
+- Reconciliation compares current balances in home currency (each transaction at its own rate) with the ledger; exchange differences on foreign customers can show as a difference.
